+WASTE's resident-trunk plus streamed-expert-bank architecture is compatible in
+principle with the Inkling family:
+
+- routed experts can remain disk-streamed and cache-managed;
+- shared experts must remain resident because every token uses them;
+- attention, normalization, relative-position, convolution, and routing math
+  require a new architecture path rather than reuse of KDA or MLA;
+- manifest publication must remain blocked until the new loader and forward
