+## 4. Implemented patch series
+
+### Patch 1 — source inspection and fail-closed converter dispatch
+
+- explicit Inkling architecture identification;
+- dependency-free config, index, shard-header, tokenizer, processor, and chat
+  template inventory;
+- exact provenance labels: confirmed from config, inferred from weights,
+  inferred from code, or unknown;
+- refusal to pass an Inkling source through the Kimi converter.
+
+### Patch 2 — deterministic conversion plan
+
+- derives every layer descriptor from the source config;
+- separates local/global attention and dense/sparse MLP layers;
+- inventories resident tensors, streamed routed experts, shared experts, and
+  deferred MTP/vision/audio assets;
+- validates every required tensor shape before payload conversion;
+- writes only `conversion-plan.json` in `--plan-only` mode;
+- retains an explicitly synthetic 42-layer candidate fixture solely to prove
+  that the planner is parameterized.
+
+### Patch 3 — bounded source adapter and C math primitives
+
+- lazy sharded safetensors reader for BF16, F16, and F32;
+- bounded axis-0 expert reads;
+- exact fused gate/up transforms for dense, routed, and shared weights;
+- standalone dependency-free C implementations of routing, relative bias,
+  global log scaling, and cached depthwise short convolution;
+- PyTorch/C differential tests.
+
+### Patch 4 — routed-expert BF16 staging and runtime guard
+
+- one routed expert at a time;
+- one 4 KiB-aligned record containing gate, up, and down BF16 payloads;
+- fixed header, payload CRC32, source-hash sidecars, atomic publication, and
+  resumable verified banks;
+- no WEXP/VQ claim and no `manifest.json`;
+- architecture classification in both memory planning and model loading;
+- explicit unsupported status until an Inkling forward path exists.
+
+For any supplied config, staged expert payload bytes are:
+
+```text
+3 * hidden_size * routed_intermediate_size * 2
+```
+
+The record size is that payload plus the 64-byte staging header, rounded up to
+4 KiB. No Small-specific record size is asserted before Small's config exists.
+
+### Patch 5 — resident trunk staging and C configuration contract
+
+- streams large identity tensors in bounded chunks, including embeddings and
+  unembedding weights;
+- deinterleaves dense and shared fused gate/up tensors in one source pass;
+- publishes one atomic canonical tensor artifact and source-bound sidecar per
+  resident tensor;
+- verifies shape, dtype, target identity, file geometry, and CRC;
+- resumes verified artifacts without reading source payloads again;
+- publishes `trunk-stage.json` last, while keeping `trunk.bin` and
+  `manifest.json` absent;
+- adds a dependency-free `waste_inkling_config` builder that validates all
+  dimensions and derives every layer's exact local/global geometry;
+- adds an overflow-checked decode memory contract for:
+  - local-window and global K/V caches;
+  - all four convolution rings per layer;
+  - token vectors, Q/K/V/relative projections, attention scores, routing,
+    routed expert workspace, dense/shared activations, and logits.
+
+The public WASTE planner remains guarded. The new Inkling memory helper is not
+used for `waste_open()` until loader tensor validation and the actual allocator
+implement the same field-by-field contract.
